, HAPPY HOUR WHOA"},{"business_id":"W3vh-SwbjqvTWczrDOsKgA","review_id":"vh4yg3opysXQX7G1QVNQYw","date":"2013-06-02T12:23:44","stars":4,"text_representativeness":0.9426392316818237,"text_excerpt":"It's worth going for the sushi happy hour. The food is generally on the expensive side, but it's definitely high quality. I love this place, but unfortunately the negative comments about service are deserved. Service aside, the sushi here is better than most places in NOLA."},{"business_id":"W3vh-SwbjqvTWczrDOsKgA","review_id":"Qy_muV2Jyqobdn1tG-L_qA","date":"2013-07-26T17:41:36","stars":5,"text_representativeness":0.9398351311683655,"text_excerpt":"After eating at a much-belauded sushi restaurant in Houston last weekend (and leaving more than mystified), I truly felt the need to hit up Chiba with that recent memory of overpriced/hyped Japanese food still fresh in my mind. And by \"need\" I mean that we didn't even stop home first after a long ass road trip home. I ordered the same exact items as the first time (mushroom gyoza; soy paper-wrapped tempura roll and cucumber/avocado roll), with an addition, the ginger sautéed green beans (DIEVINE). Verdict was the same as last time: favorite sushi restaurant in NOLA, but hey Chiba, thanks for being creative, urbane *and* uh, approachable. It's nice to be in a slightly upscale (while incred..."}],"visual":[{"business_id":"W3vh-SwbjqvTWczrDOsKgA","photo_id":"E19PZ4Y_Eren00l74R3vjg","label":"food","image_url":"/photos/E19PZ4Y_Eren00l74R3vjg.jpg","visual_representativeness":0.8878598213195801},{"business_id":"W3vh-SwbjqvTWczrDOsKgA","photo_id":"KDX_ieT3QgQlOZaRXl10VA","label":"food","image_url":"/photos/KDX_ieT3QgQlOZaRXl10VA.jpg","visual_representativeness":0.8848737478256226},{"business_id":"W3vh-SwbjqvTWczrDOsKgA","photo_id":"cYvBon29vzwj59FGhRg-gQ","label":"inside","image_url":"/photos/cYvBon29vzwj59FGhRg-gQ.jpg","visual_representativeness":0.8834278583526611},{"business_id":"W3vh-SwbjqvTWczrDOsKgA","photo_id":"9edSwjcWahW7g8j